 "text": "GIS - Williams County, ND\nYou are using an outdated browser. Please upgrade your browser to improve your experience.\nSkip to content\nSkip to navigation\nSite map\nAction toolbar\nPayments\nTranslate\nTranslate language select\nSelect language Afrikaans Albanian Amharic Arabic Armenian Azerbaijani Basque Belarusian Bengali Bosnian Bulgarian Catalan Cebuano Chichewa Chinese (Simplified) Chinese (Traditional) Corsican Croatian Czech Danish Dutch English Esperanto Estonian Filipino Finnish French Frisian Galician Georgian German Greek Gujarati Haitian Creole Hausa Hawaiian Hebrew Hindi Hmong Hungarian Icelandic Igbo Indonesian Irish Italian Japanese Javanese Kannada Kazakh Khmer Korean Kurdish (Kurmanji) Kyrgyz Lao Latin Latvian Lithuanian Luxembourgish Macedonian Malagasy Malay Malayalam Maltese Maori Marathi Mongolian Myanmar (Burmese) Nepali Norwegian Pashto Persian Polish Portuguese Punjabi Romanian Russian Samoan Scottish Gaelic Serbian Sesotho Shona Sindhi Sinhala Slovak Slovenian Somali Spanish Sundanese Swahili Swedish Tajik Tamil Telugu Thai Turkish Ukrainian Urdu Uzbek Vietnamese Welsh Xhosa Yiddish Yoruba Zulu\nSearch\nWilliams County, ND\nMenu\nPrimary menu links\nGovernment\nCalendar\nContact\nNews\nService Request\nAction toolbar\nPayments\nSearch\nWilliams County, ND\nGIS\nContact\n(701) 713-3400\nContact us\nPhysical Address (and FedEx/UPS)\nWilliams County Administration Building, 2nd Floor\n206 E Broadway\nWilliston, ND 58801\nMailing Address\nP.O. Box 2047\nWilliston, ND 58802-2047\nMonday – Friday: 8 am – 5 pm\nAbout\nDepartment Head: Helen Askim, County Administrator\nGIS Analysts: Ryan Miles, Rafael Hauge\nWilliams County uses Geographic Information Systems (GIS) for managing and developing spatial data about infrastructure like roads, district boundaries, and property in the County. The Department produces printed maps and web maps using specialized geospatial software.\nThe data is available for download and exploration by the public and County staff.\nDownload GIS Data\nRequest an Address\nDepartment Maps\nRoad Maps\nVector Control Spray Blocks\nPlanning & Zoning Maps\nSubdivision Viewer\nZoning & Conditional Use Permits\nDistrict Boundary Maps\nFind your local representative\nFind your local County Commissioner or Legislative member\nPrecinct and Polling Locations Map\nFire and Ambulance Districts\nSchool Districts\nAs of July 1, 2026\nTax Districts\nAs of July 1, 2026\nProperty Maps\nAddress and Parcel Explorer\nThis new map provides the combined functionality of the Master Address Viewer and Parcel Viewer.\nDevelopment Information\nFind parcel ownership, zoning, and taxing district information all in one place.\nHistorical Imagery\nPrinted Maps\nThe GIS Department will print Williams County maps on demand for a small fee. Custom sized maps are priced based on square footage.\nSize |\nPrice w/o Imagery |\nPrice w/ Imagery |\n24\" x 36\" (6 sq. ft) |\n$5.00 |\n$7.00 |\n36\" x 48\" (12 sq. ft) |\n$5.00 |\n$13.00 |\n42\" x 54\" (15.75 sq. ft) |\n$7.00 |\n$17.00 |\nAcceptable forms of payment include check (made out to Williams County), credit card ($3 processing fee), or cash (exact change). Payment can be made at the Development Services counter on the 2nd floor of the Willliams County Administration Building upon pick up.\nHelpful\n-->\nShare\nFacebook\nTwitter\nEmail\n-->\nSize\n+\nReset\na\n−\nWelcome\nAbout\nNews\nJob Openings\nContact\nContact a Department or Official\nContact the Court System\nFind a Building Location\nAuditor’s Office: (701) 577-4500\nHours: Monday – Friday\n8:00 am – 5:00 pm CT\nConnect\nHelp\nService Request\nAccessibility\nSitemap\nPowered by\n1 --> Get answers\nMy services\nMake a payment\nService Request\n1 -->\nSelect question type\nTransportation\nProperty & Housing\nCulture & Recreation\nClose window\nSearch Site\nSearch\nClose window",
